  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can express the ratio of the number of rectangles to the number of kites as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of rectangles}:\\text{number of kites}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of rectangles. There are $2$ rectangles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of kites. There are $5$ kites.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of rectangles to kites is $2:5.$\n\nTherefore, the missing numbers are $5$ and $2.$",
